// The game's music: a piano song built on Ryan's melody, played by engine::piano. Ryan played the
// melody on the keys (2026-10-22: keys/takes.wrela's take 1) and asked for "a whole new song around
// my melody and the tempo i set", the earlier song ripped out.
//
// The melody: a falling "re, do, sol" (D, C, G) answered by a held E; again, answered by a B tied
// over the bar; again a beat late; and "fa, fa, mi, re", the D ringing on. His notes fit a grid of
// 109 quarter notes a minute to within a few hundredths of a beat, so that is the tempo, and his
// four bars are the theme as he played them, every note in his order. He liked "the core vibe" and
// asked for more ("some jazz or harmonics are cool"), so Claude wrote the rest round them as
// Japanese city pop does, jazz harmony over a straight, laid-back groove:
// - the chords: C major 9, A minor 9, D minor 9, G13 under his bars, so his "fa, fa, mi, re" is
//   G13's seventh, thirteenth and fifth; then E minor 7, A7 (his C over it the blue sharp nine),
//   D minor 9 to G13, and home to C major 9. They're voiced without their roots, the third,
//   seventh and ninth in the left hand, and the bass plays the root;
// - a four-bar answer that turns the motif over and comes home ("sol, si, la" sliding up into the
//   A7; "do, ti, sol, mi; fa, mi, re, la, ti; do");
// - a bridge built from his "fa, fa, mi, re" in a sequence (F major 9, E minor 7, E7, A minor 9;
//   D minor 9, G13, F major 9, G9 suspended);
// - the shimmer: a fourth voice, high arpeggios of the chords' ninths and thirteenths at a phrase's
//   end, like bells;
// - the grooves.
//
// One pass is 38 bars, 84 seconds:
// - the intro (4 bars): the motif twice, high and sparse, and his "fa, fa, mi, re", over the
//   theme's first four chords, the shimmer answering;
// - the theme (8 bars): his four bars and the answer, mezzo-forte, the bass on 1, the "and" of 2
//   and 3, and the chords on 2 and the "and" of 4, laid back;
// - the bridge (8 bars): his figure on A, B, E, then F, G, A, rising to forte, the bass in long
//   notes and then pumping eighths;
// - the chorus (8 bars, twice): the theme an octave up in octaves, forte, over a syncopated bass in
//   octaves and chords on the off-beats;
// - the turn (2 bars): the motif twice over D minor 9 and G13, back to the intro.
// The form is code (`looped`): the game plays `PASSES` passes (10 minutes), then the motif and a
// C major hit.
//
// The playing is tight and on the beat: the pushes accented, everything not tied short and
// bouncing, a light pedal.
//
// The game's main makes the music's piano once (`music`), on the program's thread, and gives it to
// the game's voice (sound.wrela), which plays it with the game's sounds over it.

use engine::perform::{Mark, Pedal, PedalPoint, Performance, Played, Taste, bar, perform}
use engine::piano::{Piano, piano, play_piano}
use engine::piano_grand::GRAND
use engine::score::{Level, Score, meter, score}
use std::audio::SAMPLE_RATE
use std::collections::Vec

/// The intro: the motif twice, high and sparse, and his "fa, fa, mi, re", over the theme's first
/// chords, the shimmer answering.
const INTRO = score("intro", meter(beats: 4, unit: 4))
    .voice(
        "melody",
        [
            "r/2 d6/8 !mp c6 g5/4 | r/1 |",
            "r/2 d6/8 c6 g5/4 | f5/4. f5/8 e5/4 d5/4 |",
        ],
    )
    .voice(
        "chords",
        [
            "r/4 <e3 g3 b3 d4>/4 r/4 r/8 <e3 g3 b3 d4>/8 |",
            "r/4 <c3 e3 g3 b3>/4 r/4 r/8 <c3 e3 g3 b3>/8 |",
            "r/4 <f3 a3 c4 e4>/4 r/4 r/8 <f3 a3 c4 e4>/8 |",
            "r/4 <f3 b3 e4>/4 r/4 r/8 <f3 b3 e4>/8 |",
        ],
    )
    .voice(
        "bass",
        [
            "c2/4 r/8 c2/8 g2/4 r/4 | a1/4 r/8 a1/8 e2/4 r/4 |",
            "d2/4 r/8 d2/8 a2/4 r/4 | g1/4 r/8 g1/8 d2/4 r/4 |",
